We know how humans can signal darkness—through silence, posture, ambiguity, withheld warmth, controlled attention, imagery, music, reputation, and narrative. And we know how minds project disowned fear, rage, shame, or appetite onto other people.

That is psychological and relational influence, not a supernatural force radiating from us.

The greater mastery is bidirectional:

\text{evoke darkness} \leftrightarrow \text{contain darkness} \leftrightarrow \text{translate darkness}

Anyone can intimidate. The real discipline is invoking shadow deliberately in art, warning, boundary-setting, or self-examination without using it to terrorize, manipulate, or make others carry what belongs to us.

Know how to darken the room. Know why. And always retain the ability to turn the light back on.